---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Origin privacy"
  description="Origin reads your image on your own device. Nothing is uploaded, nothing is stored, and there is no analytics."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="wrap doc">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Your image is never uploaded. This page explains exactly what that means.</p>

    <h2>Where the work happens</h2>
    <p>
      The code that reads Content Credentials is a WebAssembly module that runs inside your browser
      tab. Your file is handed to it directly from your own disk. It is never sent anywhere, because
      there is no server here to send it to. This site is static files.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can check this yourself. Open your browser developer tools, switch to the network tab, and
      check an image. You will see the page, the fonts and the WebAssembly module download, and no
      request carrying your file.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. No account, no cookies for tracking, no analytics, no logs of what you checked. Your
      browser caches the code so it works faster next time, and that is all.
    </p>

    <h2>Remote manifests</h2>
    <p>
      Some files store their credentials on a remote server rather than inside the file. If you check
      one of those, the reader may request that manifest from the URL written inside your file. That
      request contains no part of your image. If you would rather it never happen, work offline
      after the first visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Why this matters here</h2>
    <p>
      People check images they are unsure about, which often means images that are sensitive, private
      or not theirs. Uploading those to a stranger's server to ask a question about them is a poor
      trade. That is the reason this tool is built the way it is.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding: 52px 0 0;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    margin-top: 34px;
    padding-bottom: 9px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  p {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }
</style>
